0073 - RAM text for GLQuake's flash-resident kernel code: MEASURED, REJECTED (2026-09-27)
====================================================================================

NOT SHIPPED. The Makefile default stays the 0069 list; the board runs #393.

Question: GLQuake (QuakeSpasm timedemo, fullscreen 320x240) spends 9.1% of
hart-1 PC samples in kernel code that still executes from XIP flash, and fps
tracks hart-1 I-refills (memory s31-icache-geometry). Does moving the densest
of that code into RAM text help?

Samples: 4 x 8,000 h1s captures on #393 (artifacts/gl/glquake/prof9, and
kfast/prof10a-c: glquake-run.sh GQ_PROF=60 GQ_PROFN=2, 8.6/8.9/8.6 fps),
resolved against `nm -nS vmlinux` of #397 - the #393 source rebuilt, every
symbol at the same address as ship-393-System.map (the port tree's 0072
pie-log diagnostic shifts 29,430 symbols, so it was swapped out for the
build) - and a regenerated function index (kfast/fn-index-397.txt,
kfast/mk-fn-index.sh). 2,909 of 32,000 samples in flash text; the largest
flash items cannot move (handle_exception/ret_from_exception/call_on_irq_stack
and __fstate_* are assembly, arch_cpu_idle is WFI, memcpy/memset and
esp32s31_cache_* implement the copy or maintain the caches,
fallback_scalar_usercopy_sum_enabled is uaccess.S).

List: gq-pick.list = fastfn-pick.py at an 8 kB budget with the 0069 list
excluded (91 functions, 8,126 B, 851 samples = 2.7% of all; 4 kB would
cover 2.1%, 12 kB 3.0%, 16 kB 3.1%) minus arch_dma_cache_wback and
esp32s31_lcd_flush_range (cache maintenance stays in flash; the picker now
forbids them) = 89 functions, 7,914 B; plus gq-extra.list, 8 static
duplicates the picker skips as ambiguous, resolved to their object by their
flash neighbours (rcu_qs, the CLIC's mmiowb_set_pending, kernel/irq/chip.o's
__raw_spin_unlock/mmiowb_spin_unlock/irqd_set, div64.o and build_policy.o's
div_u64_rem, fs/file.o's files_lookup_fd_raw: ~143 samples). Top by
samples: __snd_pcm_lib_xfer, switch_mm, account_user_time, snd_pcm_ioctl,
__accumulate_pelt_segments, esp32s31_ahb_irq, riscv_sched_clock.
agg-hot-swap-gq.list/.lds.h = 0069 + extras + pick. Kernel #398: RAM text
+7,024 B, flash _etext -3,328 B; fastfn-verify: all moved except the
__sched functions (schedule_timeout family, down_read, mutex_lock/unlock)
and tick_check_broadcast_expired. Boots clean.

A/B (fresh boot per run, one timedemo each, GQ_CC=1, interleaved B A A B B A A B B A):
  #393  8.7 9.0 8.9 8.8 8.2   median 8.80 mean 8.72   hart-1 I-refills 40.2-55.0 k/frame (mean 45.4)
  #398  8.3 8.6 8.8 8.9 8.7   median 8.70 mean 8.66   hart-1 I-refills 42.2-52.8 k/frame (mean 47.7)
No gain: the arms overlap completely and #398's hart-1 I-refills are not
lower - moving 2.7% of samples' worth of code does not shrink the working
set the game and libGL compete for. The cold control (agg-cold-swap-gq,
#399: 73 zero-sample functions, 8,204 B, RAM +7,888 B) was built but not
run - the hot result was not ambiguous in its favour.
Raw: artifacts/gl/glquake/kfast/ (ab.log, ab-summary.txt) and
artifacts/gl/glquake/arms/kf-*.
